SHA-256 Verification Commands



Linux & macOS (Terminal)

Option A: Verify specific downloaded file using grep

curl -sO https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/156.0/SHA256SUMS
grep "YOUR_FILENAME" SHA256SUMS | sha256sum -c -


cd ~/Downloads
curl -sO https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/156.0/SHA256SUMS
grep "mac/en-US/Firefox 156.0.dmg" SHA256SUMS | shasum -a 256 -c -



Here is the complete command for the file already sitting in your Downloads folder at /Users/computer/downloads/'Firefox 156.0.dmg:

curl -sO "https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/156.0/SHA256SUMS" && \
grep "mac/en-US/Firefox 156.0.dmg" SHA256SUMS | sed 's|mac/en-US/||' | shasum -a 256 -c -


curl -sO "https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/156.0/SHA256SUMS" && \
grep "mac/en-US/Firefox 156.0.dmg" SHA256SUMS | sed 's|mac/en-US/||' | sha256sum -c -




Here is the complete, single-block command sequence you can copy and paste into your terminal. 
It changes to your Downloads directory, downloads both the SHA256SUMS file and the Firefox DMG, strips the folder path, and verifies the file:

cd ~/Downloads && \
curl -sL "https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/156.0/mac/en-US/Firefox%20156.0.dmg" -o "Firefox 156.0.dmg" && \
curl -sO "https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/156.0/SHA256SUMS" && \
grep "mac/en-US/Firefox 156.0.dmg" SHA256SUMS | sed 's|mac/en-US/||' | shasum -a 256 -c -


or


cd ~/Downloads && \
rm -f "Firefox 156.0.dmg" && \
curl -sL "https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/156.0/mac/en-US/Firefox%20156.0.dmg" -o "Firefox 156.0.dmg" && \
curl -sO "https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/156.0/SHA256SUMS" && \
grep "mac/en-US/Firefox 156.0.dmg" SHA256SUMS | sed 's|mac/en-US/||' | shasum -a 256 -c -














