SHA-512 Verification Commands


Linux & macOS (Terminal)

Option A: Verify specific downloaded file using grep

curl -sO https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/156.0/SHA512SUMS
grep "YOUR_FILENAME" SHA512SUMS | sha512sum -c -


Option B: Compare calculated hash manually

sha512sum YOUR_FILENAME

shasum -a 512 "Firefox Setup 156.0.dmg"


Windows (PowerShell)

Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA512 .\YOUR_FILENAME





GPG Signature Verification (Optional)
To verify that the checksum file itself was authentically signed by Mozilla:



# Download checksum file and signature
curl -sO https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/156.0/SHA256SUMS
curl -sO https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/156.0/SHA256SUMS.asc

# Import Mozilla release key from directory
curl -sO https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/156.0/KEY
gpg --import KEY

# Verify signature
gpg --verify SHA256SUMS.asc SHA256SUMS






